{"type":"npc","name":"Dewdrop Ooze","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":300,"temp":0,"max":300,"details":""},"ac":{"value":18,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":10}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"acid","exceptions":[]},{"type":"critical-hits","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]},{"type":"visual","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"sonic","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"fire","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":10},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>While most oozes dwell in dank dungeons and festering swamps, the dewdrop ooze has adapted to far more pleasant climes. Typically taking on the appearance of crystal-clear water, these oozes have mastered the art of camouflage and populate natural areas such as lakefronts, forests, and river valleys. In areas where standing water is typically tinged with dust, sand, or mud, dewdrop oozes absorb these local particles into their bodies.</p><p>Dewdrop oozes do not actively hunt prey. Instead, they scatter their bodies, hoping for unsuspecting creatures to step within their range. When the opportune moment arrives, they regroup around the target, capturing them unawares and imprisoning them within their acidic body. By hiding among the condensation that gathers on the grass at dawn or the moisture dripping from stalactites, dewdrop oozes can mount a deadly ambush on even the most seasoned adventurer. They sometimes perch upon the webs of giant spiders, concealing themselves in the hopes of poaching a meal or even gobbling up the spider itself.</p><p>Luckily, dewdrop oozes are notoriously sedentary. Rather than chasing down creatures that flee their grasp, they scatter their bodies into tiny droplets again, resetting their deadly trap. Once they find a meal, they disincorporate, leaving enough droplets on the body to digest it while allowing the rest of their forms to catch additional prey. While dewdrop oozes do not seek companionship from their own kind, they sometimes cluster together in favorable hunting grounds, creating a deadly gauntlet.</p><p>Dewdrop oozes are particularly vulnerable to loud noises. Upon contact with powerful soundwaves, the oozes reflexively reform, revealing themselves and spoiling any potential ambush. A prudent adventurer wanting to avoid an encounter with dewdrop oozes ought to keep a thunderstone or similar item in their back pocket. These masters of camouflage can also be exposed by the uncanny sight of their recent prey, partially digested corpses slick with acid dew.</p><h2>Sum of Parts</h2><p>Even a single dewdrop separated from its whole remains animate, and individual droplets are sometimes bought and sold as curiosities. Strangely, lone dewdrops seem to recognize the ooze from which they were formed and refuse to join with other oozes. This peculiar behavior has led some naturalists to speculate that dewdrop oozes are more intelligent than they appear, or that they have been imbued with self-identity by an elemental—or perhaps even divine—power.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 125/275/500 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), perception item, skill items (Athletics)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> acid, bane, constitution, energy resistant (acid, fire, vitality), fortification, music, poison, poisonous armor, strength, throwing, water, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Victoria Sullivan","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":-3},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":-5},"wi